288+  02D7              ; -------------------------------------------------------------------------
289+  02D7              ; Unified guest memory interface
290+  02D7              ;
291+  02D7              ; Guest physical address is classified before selecting its physical backing:
292+  02D7              ;   00000-9FFFF / C8000-FDFFF : guest RAM, pages 44h-83h
293+  02D7              ;   A0000-BFFFF               : linear VGA aperture backing, pages 30h-37h
294+  02D7              ;   C0000-C7FFF               : VGA BIOS slot, pages 20h-21h
295+  02D7              ;   FE000-FFFFF               : system BIOS slot, page 10h (8 KiB image)
296+  02D7              ;
297+  02D7              ; The VGA aperture backend is deliberately a byte-linear staging layer over
298+  02D7              ; the first 128 KiB of the 256 KiB VRAM allocation. It is NOT yet IBM VGA
299+  02D7              ; plane/latch/read-mode/write-mode emulation. VGA register semantics are a
300+  02D7              ; separate implementation stage.
301+  02D7              ;
302+  02D7              ; All backing is reached through WIN3. A is the page bias for the address
303+  02D7              ; formula: page = (guest_high_nibble*4)+(guest_middle>>6)+bias.
304+  02D7              ; -------------------------------------------------------------------------
